    "explanation": "Both sides are substantially right, and the case settles on the platform's own numbers. To the rider: the $4.00 cancellation fee cannot stand and is refunded in full. The driver ended the trip with reason code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE. POL-NS-01(d) recognises only RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE and EXCESSIVE_WAIT, and the clause calls DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE the driver's own admission that he could not find you, routing such a trip to POL-NS-03. Independently, POL-NS-01(b) fails: on the GPS trace (EV-GPS-00206, 52 fixes, 100% coverage, no sampling gap over 120 s) none of the driver's fixes lies inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius (0 qualifying in-radius fixes) and his closest approach over the whole trace is 284.95 m, so he never entered the POL-NS-02 geofence. POL-NS-06's arithmetic agrees: in-geofence dwell is 0 s against the 300 s LARGE_VENUE minimum, a 300 s shortfall, and with 0 separate in-geofence intervals there is no second interval for the limb (i) accumulation rule to add; the only advisory that could ever excuse anything is MISSING (EV-ADVIS-00206-01, payload null, weight 0.0), citable as an absence but establishing no kerb restriction, enforcement, closure or accident. The fare line reconciles exactly under fee_schedule.resolution_rule (LARGE_VENUE $4.00 vs RYDE_X $4.00, greater $4.00), so there is no POL-NS-08(d) defect and the refund is the whole $4.00. To the driver: your closest approach of 284.95 m is outside the 120 m arrival radius but inside POL-NS-03's 400 m ceiling, and you held there for the 6.6 minutes the trip record shows (395 s against the 300 s minimum), so this is a wrong-face-of-the-venue hold, not a rider no-show — exactly what your own account of being placed at the HarbourFront kerb describes. Fault is allocated from the chat log alone: neither party posted a message naming an entrance, block, tower or bay (the log holds only the two SYSTEM notifications, and its 2 messages reconcile with trip_record.chat_message_count), while trip_record.registered_pickup_points is 4. POL-NS-03(ii) therefore attributes the mislocation to pin ambiguity and awards you a platform-funded goodwill payment of 50 per cent of the $4.00 fee — $2.00 — charged to the platform and never recovered from the rider. That is not the $3.20 POL-NS-07 would pay: POL-NS-07 requires POL-NS-01 to be satisfied in full and it is not, so the anti-farming check is never reached, and POL-NS-07 never licenses money to the rider in any event. Per POL-GEN-03 the rider's $4.00 refund and your $2.00 goodwill are independent and are not netted. On the points that could have changed the result: POL-NS-05's false-arrival route does not bite — the 15:12:05 arrival marker sits inside the clause's own carve-out (stationary within 300 m of the pin, closest approach 284.95 m, but outside the arrival radius), so the marker is not false and no POL-NS-05(ii) false-arrival record is referred. POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider, because the chat log contains no rider message and limb (a) cannot be run; the refund rests on the GPS and POL-NS-03, not on POL-NS-04. POL-NS-09 does not trigger: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 on both profiles, the anti-farming check does not trip (1 no-show termination against 187 completed trips), and no artifact carrying a deciding fact is impaired under POL-NS-08(a)-(d) — the arrived timestamp falls inside the trace with no clock skew, there are 52 driver fixes with no >120 s gap, the chat reconciles with the recorded message count, and the fare line reconciles. I also considered whether the 8.5-minute interval between the two system messages engages POL-NS-08(c); it does not, because the second message is the arrival notification generated at the arrival marker itself (15:12:06, one second after the 15:12:05 marker), so the arrival moment is captured and the log reconciles in count and sequence. The only artifact below full weight is the missing advisory (weight 0.0), which carries no deciding fact here and so does not lower confidence. Both parties' profiles are credibility context only and have not been used as a ground of decision (POL-GEN-01)."
