    "explanation": "The $4.00 cancellation fee is refunded to the rider in full, and the driver receives a $2.00 platform-funded goodwill payment. The two are independent and are not netted against each other.\n\nWhy the fee cannot stand. A no-show fee is chargeable only if all four conditions of POL-NS-01 hold, and two of them fail. First, the trip was terminated with cancellation_reason_code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE - the driver's own statement that he could not find the rider - and POL-NS-01(d) recognises only RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT; the clause says in terms that such a trip is decided under POL-NS-03. Second, on the driver's own GPS trace (EV-GPS-00206, weight 1.0) none of the 52 fixes between 15:03:30 and 15:18:40 falls inside the 120 m arrival radius for a LARGE_VENUE pickup, and the closest approach to the pin is 284.95 m. Under POL-NS-02 the driver never arrived, so limb (b) fails as well.\n\nWhy this is a wrong-entrance case (POL-NS-03). The closest approach of 284.95 m sits outside the 120 m arrival radius but inside POL-NS-03's 400 m ceiling, and inside the 300 m line that would otherwise have made the 15:12:05 arrival marker false under POL-NS-05. The driver's account and the 6.6-minute wait in the trip record (EV-TRIP-00206, weight 1.0) place him holding at the HarbourFront kerb while the pin sat at VivoCity Lobby L. The pickup therefore failed at the wrong face of the venue: POL-NS-01(b) fails and the whole $4.00 cancellation fee returns to the rider. The system message 'Your driver has arrived' at 15:12:06 was sent while the driver's trace shows he was never inside the arrival radius, and that mislocation cannot be laid at the rider's door.\n\nWho bears the cost. Fault is allocated from the chat log (EV-CHAT-00206, weight 1.0), which holds only two SYSTEM messages. The rider never named an entrance, block, tower or bay, so POL-NS-03(i) does not apply. Neither party specified a sub-location and the trip record shows registered_pickup_points of 4 - two or more - so POL-NS-03(ii) attributes the mislocation to pin ambiguity, not to either party, and the driver receives a platform-funded goodwill payment of 50 percent of the $4.00 fee, that is $2.00, charged to the platform and never recovered from the rider. The rider's own presence is consistent with the account: EV-GPS-00206 places the rider's device no more than 22.5 m from the pin, well inside the 150 m LARGE_VENUE rider-presence radius.\n\nPoints that do not change the outcome. POL-NS-07's 80 percent compensation (SGD 3.20 of SGD 4.00) is not payable because it is conditioned on POL-NS-01 being satisfied in full, and it is not; for the same reason the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check is never reached (on the citable fields, 1 no-show termination against 187 completed trips would pass in any event). POL-NS-06's shortfall arithmetic - 0 seconds of effective in-geofence dwell against the 300-second LARGE_VENUE minimum - would independently produce the same full refund, but POL-NS-03, not POL-NS-06, fixes the driver's money. The MISSING traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00206-01, weight 0.0, disclosed) means POL-NS-06(i) accumulation cannot be run, and it would not have helped in any case because the trace shows no separate in-geofence intervals to sum. POL-NS-04 is not engaged because the rider sent no message during the waiting window. No artifact is impaired under POL-NS-08 - the trace has 100 percent coverage and no gap over 120 seconds, the chat log's 2 messages match trip_record.chat_message_count, the arrival marker falls inside the trace rather than 90 seconds away from it, and the $4.00 cancellation-fee line equals the greater of the LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee - so no PARTIAL_REFUND cap applies and confidence is set at 0.90 on deciding artifacts at full weight. No limb of POL-NS-09 is triggered, so the fee is refunded now rather than held for a reviewer: both counterparty-dispute counters are 0 and the anti-farming branch does not trip.\n\nNo referral is issued. POL-NS-05(ii)'s false-arrival record does not fire because the driver was stationary within 300 m of the pin - inside the clause's own carve-out - and no other clause produces a referral."
  },
